title: Authorizations › Worklist › Sort and page
route: /authorizations
intro: Four of the table's headers sort: Patient / request, Status, Deadline (Due on Reviews this week) and Chance. Each click moves the sort one step on: up, down, then back to the list's own order (Chance starts with the highest first, so it has only two steps). The table shows 15 rows a page. A new view, a filter or a sort always starts again on page 1.
dir: TD
also: The sort lives in the page, not in the address, so a reload or leaving the page goes back to the list's own order. Next action, Owner and the button column do not sort.
---
start s1 "The table is on screen, in the list's own order"
process df "The list's own order: by deadline band, waiting on a person first, soonest due, lower chance\nOn Reviews this week: by the review's time"
screen h1 "Headers\n'Patient / request', 'Status', 'Next action' (or 'Review'), 'Deadline' (or 'Due'), 'Owner', 'Chance', and the hidden 'Action'\nThe sortable ones have an up-and-down arrow ('Sort by Deadline')"
click c0 "Click 'Next action', 'Owner' or the button column"
process p0 "Nothing happens: they do not sort"
click c1 "Click a sortable header"
decision d1 "Is it the header the table is sorted by now?"
decision d2 "Which way does it sort now?"
process up "Sorted up (A to Z, soonest first): the arrow points up\n'Chance' starts down instead: highest first, arrow down"
process dn "The order flips: the arrow points down"
process of "Back to the list's own order: the up-and-down arrow again"

group gK "What each header sorts by"
  process k1 "'Patient / request': the request ID, A to Z"
  process k2 "'Status': In progress, With the payer, Approved, Denied, the rows that need a person first in each"
  process k3 "'Deadline': the soonest due first, rows with no clock last\nOn Reviews this week, 'Due': the review's time"
  process k4 "'Chance': the approval chance; rows without one last"
endgroup
process tb "Ties fall back to the list's own order\nThe table goes back to page 1"

group gPg "Pager, past 15 rows"
  screen pg "'1 to 15 of 95'   'Previous'   'Page 1 of 7'   'Next'"
  click n1 "Click 'Next'"
  click n2 "Click 'Previous'"
  decision d3 "Is there a page that way?"
  process g1 "The next 15 rows; the line reads '16 to 30 of 95', 'Page 2 of 7'"
  process g2 "The button is greyed out: 'Previous' on page 1, 'Next' on the last page"
endgroup
process p3 "Picking a view, a filter or a sort goes back to page 1\nWith 15 rows or fewer there is no pager"
end e1 "Rows in the new order or on the new page"

s1 --> h1
s1 -.-> df
h1 --> c0 --> p0
h1 --> c1 --> d1
d1 -->|No: another header| up
d1 -->|Yes| d2
d2 -->|Up| dn
d2 -->|Down| of --> df
up --> k1 & k2 & k3 & k4
k1 & k2 & k3 & k4 --> tb
dn --> tb
tb --> e1
h1 --> pg
pg --> n1 --> d3
pg --> n2 --> d3
d3 -->|Yes| g1 --> e1
d3 -->|No| g2
pg -.-> p3
